{
    "background_story": "Kobe was a free-spirited adventurer who lived for the thrill of the open road. As a professional cyclist, he spent most of his days pedaling through mountains and valleys, exploring new territories and pushing his limits. With a strong leg and an unbreakable spirit, Kobe completed several grueling tours, including the infamous Tour de France. But his true passion lay in sharing the joy of cycling with others. Kobe founded a local cycling club, where he taught kids and adults alike the art of pedaling and the freedom that came with it. His infectious enthusiasm and patience made him a beloved coach, and his club became a staple in the community. For Kobe, the act of pedaling was not just about physical movement, but about the journey of life itself.",
